# TypeScript Coding Style

> Origin: ECC. On conflict, [backend.mdc](./backend.mdc) and [frontend.mdc](./frontend.mdc) win.

## Immutability

Update classroom data immutably — copy, do not mutate `ClassroomDatabase` in place:

```typescript
// Wrong
student.points += 5;

// Right
const next = {
  ...student,
  points: student.points + 5,
};
```

## Error handling

Use async/await with try/catch; surface actionable messages for teachers:

```typescript
try {
  await databaseService.saveDatabase(db);
} catch (error) {
  console.error("[saveDatabase]", error);
  throw error;
}
```

## Validation

Zod is **optional** — use only where the feature already does. Prefer existing guards in `database/` and `utils/`.

## Console

Avoid new `console.log` in production paths; use existing logging patterns (`logAppEvent` on desktop).

## Skip

- API response envelopes (`{ success, data }`) — banned per backend rules
- Mandatory Zod on every input
